.Sh LABELS
.Xr mac_lomac 4
is the integrity lattice.
When speaking to an operator, say
.Sy high-integrity
and
.Sy low-integrity .
Do not say only
.Ql high
or
.Ql low
as if those were self-explanatory.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width low-integrityxx
.It high-integrity
OS and other files a lowered process must not overwrite.
Kernel:
.Ql lomac/high
.Pq subjects: Ql lomac/high(low-high) .
.It low-integrity
User files, agents, home directories, and the level a process drops to after
reading them.
Kernel:
.Ql lomac/low
for objects;
.Ql lomac/10[2]
for a process that starts already lowered.
Those are the same integrity in speech.
.It exempt
Outside the lattice.
Root
.Ql equal(equal-equal)
is exemption, not containment.
.El
.Pp
Short proof: a low-integrity process cannot overwrite a high-integrity OS
file after reading low-integrity data.
