.Em A_D ,
not a second lattice.
.Sh THESES
Deniable separately.
T1–T5 remain
.Xr pqac 7 .
.Bl -tag -width T10xx
.It T1
Membership in
.Em BQP
does not by itself produce a classical write accepted by the reference
monitor.
.It T2
.Em A_D ,
.Em A_M ,
and MMU translation are quantum-adversary-stable mediation.
They are post-quantum access control in that sense, and not post-quantum
cryptography.
.It T3
.Pq working hypothesis
Some instrument on the plant, possibly entanglement-enhanced, can
distinguish defender computation.
.It T4
If
.Em O
factors through a kernel-visible subject, T1 and T2 constrain
.Em O .
If not, T1 and T2 are silent and the property is physical non-interference.
.It T5
Quantum advantage for
.Em O
is not free, and is not Shor's corollary.
.It T6
Unrestricted
.Em A_D
is an HRU protection system; safety is undecidable.
A restricted specification
.Pq path-regex to owner, group, mode, inherit
plus a repair morphism is a different relation: intended
.Em A_D
is restored; residual owner-grants are bounded in duration.
This does not make
.Em A_D
into
.Em A_M .
.It T7
.Xr mac 4
approximates complete mediation and isolation.
Verifiability is not supplied.
A hash-chained ledger of vnode, label, and policy-morphism events is the
monitor's evidence.
The ledger object is high in
.Em L .
Tampering is a hash-collision problem
.Pq Grover halves the bits; production uses SHA-512 or SHA-3 .
That is
.Em A_auth
of the evidence, not of the subject.
The suite still does not
.Xr kldload 8
Kyber.
.It T8
Dynamic establishment is the create-time morphism.
Repair is the restore morphism when actual is not intended.
.Xr setfsmac 8
first-match and DAC first-match are combinators, not lattice operations.
Conjunction with
.Em A_M
is still not a product of proofs.
Optional prevention
.Pq Xr ugidfw 8
is a different module with a different proof
.Pq empty ruleset is allow-all .
.It T9
The ledger daemon is a subject.
If
.Em O
factors through it, T4 applies.
The ledger is not Faraday, not a naming retrofit, and not a secrecy lattice.
Recovery remains inside the isolation claim.
.It T10
.Pq required; not this pass
.Em A_M
constrains who may write.
The ledger records that a write occurred.
Neither lets a later subject confirm that the bits they read are the bits
that were written.
.Xr zfs 8
checksums detect silent corruption inside the pool; they are not a
subject-visible confirmation API.
A content digest, or a Merkle over the labeled store, bound to a ledger
checkpoint, is confirmable to the extent of the hash.
Grover halves the bits.
Next skill:
.Nm pqconfirm .
.It T11
.Pq held; open-ended; not a 1.0 requirement
A PQ-stable monitor interpreting RSA-signed code is a forged policy,
correctly enforced.
Kernel, klds, pkg, policy, and
.Xr zfs 8
send streams are code, or code-shaped.
If they are unsigned, or signed with RSA/ECC, Shor forges the input to
.Em A_M .
Authentication here is of code, not of credentials.
Redundancy is two independent reductions: ML-DSA
.Pq FIPS 204
and SLH-DSA
.Pq FIPS 205
— not two disks.
The catalog remains.
.Nm pqcode
is cut when named, not as a 1.0 gate.
Do not claim the chain is unbroken.
.It T12
.Pq gated; TPM not this pass
.Cm oneboot
is refused until the operator attests they are sufficiently satisfied that
the system is post-quantum hardened to the degree that gives them a sense of
security.
Default is no.
What the gate protects is taking the loader off the unsigned GENERIC path,
only as far as this pass can close.
TPM and measured boot are not this pass.
Changing the splash name and mark is a consequence of that attestation, not
a security claim.
Branding is not a second signature family.
Do not rebrand a box you do not yet trust.
.It T13
After install, the operator must see that POLICY, SUITE, DAC, ugidfw, login
labels, MAC overlays, and the loader config agree; must propagate a change through
all of them at once; and must read the diff of successive iterations.
Consistency is a predicate over that conjunction, not a product of proofs.
Each propagation is a named revision whose catalog hash is chained and
recorded in the ledger.
An audit that cannot show what changed is not an audit.
.Cm oneaudit ,
.Cm onepropagate .
.It T14
Claims degrade by conjunct, not as a product.
A missing or stranded protocol weakens only the claims that named it.
If the box cannot securely transport the Integrity Evidence to another host
and have that host validate the store, the off-host IE claim is degraded.
High-integrity overwrite protection, local chain, repaired
.Em A_D ,
successive policy, and the loader gate are not thereby false.
Silent
.Pq module not included
is not degraded
.Pq module included, protocol unmet .
Do not report the suite as a single bit.
.It T19
Independent reductions raise adversary cost; they do not multiply proofs.
Homogeneous copies share a layout: cache lines, vnode cache, one reduction.
Variation of data structure unshares alike semantic data
.Pq a lattice label is not a capability bitmap is not a hash-chain record is not a hash-based signature .
That inefficiency
.Pq working set, no shared fill
is why this redundancy is the valuable kind: an algorithm that has learned one representation does not find the others already in cache.
Copies of the same reduction do not count.
A cryptographic hop that is still RSA or ECC has no post-quantum resistance at that hop.
.It T20
Unlike layers do not inherit a namei TOCTOU.
A TOCTOU on path
.Em p
is inherited by a layer iff that layer re-resolves
.Em p
between check and use.
.Fn cap_enter
uses the fd; MAC on a held vnode uses
.Em vp ,
not the name.
Self-similar copies of
.Fn namei
share the race.
Stacking unlike mechanisms is not stacking boilerplate in every MAC/DAC layer.
The proof stops at directory-rename-above,
.Nm *at
races, fd passing, Casper confused-deputy.
.It T21
Federation min-cut is extra virtual dimensions of channel security.
.Em G=(V,E)
is hosts that store or validate Integrity Evidence, with an edge only on an
independent reduction
.Pq T19 .
An undetected rewrite requires a cut to every honest validator.
Size and unlike connectivity increase that cut.
They do not add bits to RSA.
Correlated hosts are not extra dimensions.
Stranded is a lost edge
.Pq T14 .
The lemma is the shape of the bound, not a number on a box.
.It T15
.Pq held
An unbroken cryptographic chain of trust is a necessary requirement of the
trusted base, distinct from T2.
Walk firmware db, loader, kernel, kld, pkg, freebsd-update, policy, rc.d,
ledger checkpoint, zfs send, replica transport.
Each hop that is cryptography must eventually be post-quantum:
ML-DSA and SLH-DSA for signatures, ML-KEM
.Pq FIPS 203
for transport, SHA-512 or SHA-3 Grover-accounted for hashes.
AES-at-rest is secrecy, not origin.
Hybrid is a transition particular; Shor still forges the classical half.
A classical or missing hop breaks the chain from that point down.
It does not un-prove high-integrity overwrite protection
.Pq T14 .
This pass catalogs the hops.
It does not claim the chain is unbroken.
.It T16
At the end of beta the system is provably secure up to the conjunction of
named bounds, and no further.
Each claimed measure states what is proven, where the proof stops, and
expected resistance against classical PPT, qubit BQP
.Pq Grover, Shor, BHT ,
qudit / non-binary quantum, and continuous-variable machines.
Mediation is n/a bits in every model.
Cryptographic particulars have numbers, already birthday- and
Grover-accounted, or an honest 0.
A zero on pkg-RSA does not zero high-integrity overwrite protection.
Empty bounds are the remainder of the work.
Do not ship
.Dq provably secure
without this sheet.
.It T17
.Nm sysutils/pqfreebsd
is the intended install path once the skills exist.
It stages; it does not
.Xr kldload 8 .
Intended operation is by a sufficiently advanced large language model that
can operate the skills
.Pq interview, Cm test* before Cm one* , Known issues, this paper .
The port cannot prove a model is advanced.
Local GPU/CPU OPTIONS:
.Nm ollama ,
.Nm llama.cpp
.Pq llama-server ,
LocalAI, llamafile, vLLM, koboldcpp.
Native path is CPU and Vulkan.
CUDA on
.Fx
is typically Linuxulator.
.Nm pqfreebsd-llm-check
finds a candidate;
.Va pqfreebsd_llm_attested=YES
is the operator's conjunct.
via-port
.Cm oneenforce
is refused without it.
That conjunct is the install path, not
.Em A_M
.Pq T14 .
Hand install from the skill tree does not set
.Pa VIA-PORT .
.It T18
Capsicum is in GENERIC.
It is not
.Xr mac 4 .
.Fn cap_enter
confines a process to the fds it already holds.
Low-integrity agents must enter.
First pass is
.Nm pqcap-enter
.Pq Fn caph_limit_stdio + Fn caph_enter + exec ,
not Casper.
Missing Capsicum does not un-prove the lattice
.Pq T14 .
Paper: Watson, Anderson, Laurie, Kennaway, USENIX Security 2010
.Lk http://www.trustedbsd.org/2010usenix-security-capsicum-website.pdf
.El
.Sh LEDGER
An empty chain is not evidence.
The first record names the policy hash, the dataset, and the hash.
.Xr audit 4
is the in-band source;
.Pa /var/audit
is not the chain.
Rotation appends a checkpoint record.
Rewrite is a bug.
Label the dataset
.Ql high
before
.Cm enforce
or it is an unlabeled hole.
If a replica module is included, a second host stores and validates HEAD.
Network-stranded transport degrades only that claim
.Pq T14 .
.Sh A_D
The spec is a restricted language: path-regex, owner, group, mode.
No arbitrary grant verbs
.Pq the HRU cut .
First-match, same combinator as
.Xr setfsmac 8 .
.Cm observe
logs;
.Cm repair
restores after the syscall
.Pq a concurrent reader may see drift ;
.Cm prevent
generates
.Xr ugidfw 8
from the same spec.
Empty ugidfw is allow-all.
.Sh SUCCESSIVE POLICY
.Cm onepropagate
regenerates DAC, ugidfw, login fragment, overlay, and splash artifacts from
POLICY, applies, and appends a catalog hash chained to the previous
revision.
.Cm oneaudit
walks consistency and the kv-diff of live versus applied.
An audit that cannot show what changed is not an audit.
.Sh CHAIN OF TRUST
Origin hops, firmware to replica, are catalogued; see the workbench
.Pa Code
page and T15.
Today the chain of origin breaks at hop 1
.Pq UEFI RSA
or earlier if unsigned.
Hash-only hops are integrity, not origin, until a PQ signature covers the
root.
.Sh BOUNDS
The beta-end sheet
.Pq T16
names, for each remaining claim, classical bits or n/a, qubit BQP, qudit,
and CVQC, what is proven, and where the proof stops.
Mediation is n/a in every model: a qudit or analog machine still writes
through the hook.
Fill the sheet as modules land.
.Sh BOOT
The claim is the gate
.Pq T12 .
.Cm oneboot
is refused while
.Va BOOT_SATISFIED
is no.
After attestation it takes the loader off unsigned GENERIC only as far as
this pass can close.
TPM is not this pass.
A Forth mark
.Pq cross by default
may replace the stock splash; that is cosmetic.
